      "what": "The researchers developed STFusioner, a traffic flow prediction model that decouples spatial and temporal features using parallel multi-head self-attention before dynamically fusing them via a bidirectional cross-attention mechanism. Evaluated on real-world datasets, the model achieves state-of-the-art performance, yielding average relative improvements of 1.34% in Mean Absolute Error, 0.77% in Root Mean Squared Error, and 1.24% in Mean Absolute Percentage Error compared to existing baselines.",
